WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.850
Here it is running.

2
00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:03.370
The customer types what's going on.

3
00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:07.790
Married in the spring, a baby, renting, hoping to buy next year.

4
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.810
Baz doesn't reach for a product.

5
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:14.550
It asks one question, then records what it learns, where each fact came from.

6
00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:18.150
Each fact sits in a defined catalogue with its source attached.

7
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:21.490
A couple of answers later, it knows the shape of the plan.

8
00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:27.130
€32,000 saved at AIB, €1,200 a month to put away, a home by next June.

9
00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:30.830
Baz offers to remember it, but nothing is kept until she taps.

10
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.270
She can review what Baz proposes before she approves it.

11
00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:38.030
The model proposes, the customer commits, the system checks.

12
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.230
The savings are elsewhere, so Baz requests access.

13
00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:48.550
With her consent, open banking brings in the available account data, salary arriving, rent going out, savings balance.

14
00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:51.370
The consent has a defined scope and expiry.

15
00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.030
She authorises it and the picture fills in.

16
00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:57.150
The consent does not authorise a payment or anything else.

17
00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:58.590
No statement to upload.

18
00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:00.530
Baz reads the permitted data.

19
00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:02.510
Now the money gets put to work.

20
00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.530
This is arithmetic, not opinion.

21
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.910
The lump sum goes into a six month fixed term, ending before she needs it.

22
00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:12.990
€200 a month into MortgageSaver to qualify for the €2,000 bonus.

23
00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:15.970
The remainder into SuperSaver at 3%.

24
00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:19.510
Roughly €430 in the first year at the rates shown.

25
00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.950
One tap starts three account applications.

26
00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:24.750
The calculation is visible and explainable.

27
00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.050
She already banks here, so she signs in.

28
00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:30.910
The prototype uses an email code, not the bank's real identity check.

29
00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:35.870
Existing customer information appears and six fields are reused across three applications.

30
00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:37.950
Here's the important thing to notice.

31
00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:42.770
SuperSaver uses the bank's published form, 499 controls.

32
00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:48.330
Baz reads the definition, fills what it knows, then asks for the rest in the form's own words.

33
00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.870
The €32,000 is still in AIB.

34
00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:55.570
She separately authorises a transfer and the money moves towards her current account here.

35
00:01:55.880 --> 00:02:00.710
Now the bank can monitor her deposit directly without relying on continued access to the other account.

36
00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:03.390
Baz will return when it reaches €40,000.

37
00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.190
In the console, the fixed term account is opened and the transfer settled.

38
00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:09.850
Back on her phone, Baz confirms what's happened.

39
00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:12.590
Now we skip ahead, the months have passed.

40
00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:17.070
The plan stays in the console, along with the milestone the bank agreed to watch.

41
00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:19.070
The balance reaches the target.

42
00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:22.650
A notification lands without exposing financial details.

43
00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:26.610
She opens it and Baz picks up exactly where they left off.

44
00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.930
The deposit is ready and it's time to revisit the mortgage.

45
00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.290
It remembers what she already told it.

46
00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:33.590
Nothing asked twice.

47
00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:35.710
And the other side of the glass.

48
00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.750
Every case, every fact and its source.

49
00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:41.910
Linked accounts, transfers, the monitored balance.

50
00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:45.070
Guardrails ahead of the model, not inside it.

51
00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:47.750
Persona controls for style, not policy.

52
00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:50.330
Analytics built from recorded events.

53
00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:54.150
Operations and controls, built in from day one.
